# How to cite this repository. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository" on the
# repository page, and Zenodo uses it for the DOI of each release.
# When the UBD paper is published, add it under "preferred-citation" (type:
# article, with its authors, title, journal, year and doi) so that it becomes
# the citation GitHub suggests, and keep this entry for the software itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "JIBE health microsimulation: health data preparation, microsimulation engine and outputs for Greater Manchester and Melbourne"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jibeproject/health_microsim"
abstract: >-
  Health data preparation (disease incidence, mortality and prevalence rates)
  for Greater Manchester and Melbourne, an individual-level health
  microsimulation driven by the exposures (physical activity, air pollution,
  noise and greenspace) of the JIBE transport and land-use model, and the
  processing and interactive app for the model's health, exposure and travel
  outputs.
keywords:
  - health impact assessment
  - microsimulation
  - transport
  - physical activity
  - air pollution
  - noise
  - greenspace
  - Greater Manchester
  - Melbourne
